# dev.env - the DEVELOPMENT environment of this serve, complete: the production environment (every line of prod.env, scripts/check-env.py enforces it) plus the
# candidates under test. KNOBS=dev applies the three sections below (runtime, recipe, candidates). Same format as prod.env. A candidate leaves this file by promotion (its line goes into
# prod.env's recipe section, with its cells, in the same commit) or by deletion when its cells say no; a settings change for production never starts here
# without a rule written before the rows (scripts/queue-scores/decide84.py for the recipe's queues). `diff scripts/env/prod.env scripts/env/dev.env` is the
# list of what is being tried.
#
# --- runtime
# The runtime, applied by every KNOBS mode (off included): the production stack's NCCL shape (ai-engine serve4.sh's measured set: P2P and SHM off, 4
# channels, cross-NIC routing, GID 3, the four RoCE HCAs, a LAN socket name) so a boot here and a production boot are comparable, and the
# serve's fixed model settings. serve.sh adds what depends on the boot: rank, world, memory reserve and NCCL_COMM_ID. A caller's own
# NCCL_IB_HCA or NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME in the launching environment wins over the lines here (serve.sh's CALLER_WINS).
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
TENSORFOLD_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1
TF_GLM_HEAD_BITS=8
TF_GLM_DENSE_BITS=4
NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=1
NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=1
NCCL_MIN_NCHANNELS=4
NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=4
NCCL_CROSS_NIC=1
NCCL_IB_SUBNET_AWARE_ROUTING=1
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3
NCCL_IB_HCA=roceP2p1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f1,rocep1s0f0,rocep1s0f1
NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=enP7s7
#
# --- recipe
# The adopted recipe, as prod.env has it, line for line:
# KDA_PAD to MLA_FUSEMERGE: the arm measured together (docs/OVERNIGHT-2026-11-12.md section 17).
TF_GLM_KDA_PAD=1
TF_GLM_OVN_KEPT_WALK=1
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_ONEPASS=1
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_DOWN4=1
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_MLPSPLIT=4
TF_GLM_OVN_MLA_FUSEMERGE=1
# Production's DFlash2 chain rule (fnc7:0.3, section 22).
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_EDGE=0.6
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_BETA=2
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_CUTS=1:0.3
# Production's routed-expert decode kernel set (section 24). The 16-pair item plan these ran beside is upstream's unconditional decode path on
# this base (upstream 4e6cdeed9 and 51a6fe02a, our PR #2044), so TF_GLM_OVN_EXL3_ITEMS has no line.
TF_EXL3_DEC_ORDER=1
TF_GLM_OVN_X3_NC=1
TF_GLM_OVN_X3_XROW=1
TF_GLM_OVN_X3_FUSEDOWN=1
# KEEP_SEQS was measured with EY_DIRECT at 1/2/4/6/8 streams (sections 30 and 34); EY_DIRECT's win is upstream's own path now.
TF_GLM_OVN_KEEP_SEQS=1
# Sets no speed cell: it is the prompt production sends. A thinking-off request renders without its default `Reasoning Effort: Max` line, so
# its replies are not token-identical to the knob-off ones by design.
TF_GLM_OVN_OFF_EFFORT_LINE=1
# The last seven joined together (sections 45 to 49 and the queue71 and queue72 records in docs/KNOBS.md): replies equal the recipe's on every
# cell and the pairs show no level slower. NO_COPY: a DFlash2 drafter's windows without copied continuations. MM_DECTILE: a decode-window
# tile variant of the matmul launch. SWIGLU_REDUCE: the reduce and the swiglu in one launch (both checked byte for byte against the default
# launches by glm-mm-ovn). ONEPASS_PIPE: the DSA block's prompt rows on the one-pass pipeline. CHUNK_SOLO=4096: upstream's one 4,096-row
# prompt step while no stream decodes. HOST_ONCE: a request rendered once. DRAFT_NOISE: a sampled stream's draft pick uses the target's keyed
# Gumbel draws (a greedy stream never reads it).
TF_GLM_OVN_NO_COPY=1
TF_GLM_OVN_MM_DECTILE=100000
TF_GLM_OVN_SWIGLU_REDUCE=1
TF_GLM_OVN_ONEPASS_PIPE=1
TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096
TF_GLM_OVN_HOST_ONCE=1
TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_NOISE=1
# Promoted from the arm that carried it through XENV: five levels with identical replies (OVERNIGHT section 87).
TF_GLM_OVN_ABSORB_VEC=1
#
# --- candidates
# The recipe N prime of queue77 (the final confirmation at 1, 2, 4, 6 and 8 streams) and the arm every later queue adds to the committed recipe:
TF_GLM_OVN_MM_WIDE=1
TF_GLM_OVN_SIDE_PRIO=1
TF_GLM_OVERLAP_PIECES=4
TF_GLM_OVN_LATENT_ROWS=2
TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_FRONT=1
TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_FFN=1
TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_MLA=1
NCCL_NCHANNELS_PER_NET_PEER=4
# Solo prompt steps end at a request start (patches/solo-cuts/0002): decide84's solo block passed it (OVERNIGHT section 68).
TF_GLM_OVN_SOLO_TO_START=1
# A restore into the sequence that kept the state copies only what a sequence rewrites (patches/restore-held): decide84's held block passed it (section 69).
TF_GLM_OVN_RESTORE_HELD=1
#
# Not a line, on purpose: TF_GLM_REQUEST_STARTS=1 is the owner's trade (a cold prompt pays a little, a warm turn and a resume much less) and stays off
# until the owner accepts it; the arms that measure it pass it through XENV.
